    {
      "id": 3,
      "attributes": {
        "title": "Route 198 Scoping Session",
        "slug": "route-198-scoping-session",
        "startingAt": "2022-07-13T21:30:00.000Z",
        "endingAt": "2022-06-29T23:30:00.000Z",
        "content": "**NOTE:** This meeting was originally intended to be held on June 29, 2022. Please note the updated date of July 13, 2022 and the updated location of the [Canisius College Science Hall](https://goo.gl/maps/pQtn95caJRyBnTnN7).\n\nThis meeting will be the same as the May 4, 2022 meeting at Buffalo State and will present four scenarios for reimagining the Scajaquada Corridor and will provide an opportunity for public comment.\n\nThe scenarios for Region Central have been developed over 12 months of research, planning, community outreach, and analysis and represents a range of possibilities for the future of mobility in the Scajaquada Corridor.\n\nThe public is invited to watch a recording of the presentation from the May 4, 2022 Public Meeting at Buffalo State; review the four scenarios; and provide feedback. Visit https://www.gbnrtc.org/regioncentral-events for more details.",
        "createdAt": "2022-06-17T17:05:10.417Z",
        "updatedAt": "2022-06-29T11:46:07.108Z",
        "publishedAt": "2022-06-25T20:16:23.833Z",
        "featuredImage": {
          "data": null
        },
        "seo": null,
        "location": null
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "attributes": {
        "title": "Presenting Plans for the Future of the Scajaquada Corridor",
        "slug": "presenting-plans-for-the-future-of-the-scajaquada-corridor",
        "startingAt": "2022-05-04T21:30:00.000Z",
        "endingAt": "2022-05-04T23:30:00.000Z",
        "content": "## How to Get There\n* Parking is available in Lot G-21\n* The closest bus stop is the NFTA Metro #3/Grant bus at Grant St. and Rockwell Road\n\nThe Greater Buffalo Niagara Regional Transportation Council (GBNRTC) [has announced](https://www.gbnrtc.org/regioncentral-events) a public meeting to present four mobility scenarios for Region Central, a.k.a. the Scajaquada Corridor. We encourage you all to attend!\n\nAs a courtesy to the organizers, they ask you <a href=\"https://www.eventbrite.com/e/region-central-public-meeting-tickets-317724912767\" target=\"_blank\">**register in advance**</a>.\n\n### Ways to Help Spread the Word\n\n1. Share this post with family and friends!\n2. Follow <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/sccoalition/\" target=\"_blank\">@SCCoalition on Instagram</a>, <a href=\"https://twitter.com/RightSize198\" target=\"_blank\">@RightSize198 on Twitter</a> and <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/sccbuffalo\" target=\"_blank\">@SCCBuffalo on Facebook</a>.\n3. Read and share our recent blog posts on [the impact of the Scajaquada Expressway](https://www.sccoalition.net/blog/the-scajaquada-expressway-causes-traffic-problems-it-doesnt-solve-them) and [walkability](https://www.sccoalition.net/blog/for-region-central-investments-in-walkability-are-a-necessity).\n\n\n[Learn more about Region Central](https://www.gbnrtc.org/regioncentral-events)",
        "createdAt": "2022-06-20T09:39:09.759Z",
        "updatedAt": "2022-11-25T23:07:43.360Z",
        "publishedAt": "2022-06-20T13:39:14.994Z",
