    {
      "id": 9,
      "attributes": {
        "title": "Scajaquada Full Circle Speaker Series - Event 3",
        "slug": "scajaquada-full-circle-speaker-series-event-3",
        "startingAt": "2024-09-17T22:00:00.000Z",
        "endingAt": "2024-09-18T00:00:00.000Z",
        "content": "[Register for this Event](https://www.eventbrite.com/e/scajaquada-full-circle-speaker-series-tickets-965309616047)  |  [View Event flyer](https://res.cloudinary.com/ihiutch/image/upload/v1725372970/Scajaquada_Full_Circle_Flyer_September_2024_019f1926c5.pdf)\n\nPlease join us at the Burchfield Penney Art Center Auditorium on Tuesdays in September for a continuing speaker series on the Scajaquada Creek Corridor that touches on all aspects of how this critical area of Buffalo waterfront has shaped the city - including the historical, environmental, cultural, and modern day changes and issues affecting the corridor.\n\nRegistration is free. Please confirm attendance for all engagements you wish to attend.\n\n## Event 3 Agenda\n\n**Part 1 \u2014 6:00 PM - 7:00 PM** \nThe Scajaquada Corridor as Economic Driver: the Bigger Picture \u2013 Paris Roselli, President of the Richardson-Olmsted Campus and Lisa Ludwig, Executive Director, Shakespeare in Delaware Park\n\nIn this presentation Scajaquada Corridor Coalition members Paris Roselli and Lisa Ludwig will highlight the recent history and context of the Scajaquada Creek Corridor and how by working together the people of Buffalo can transform this area into a more powerful economic tool for the region.\n\n**Part 1 \u2014 7:00 PM - 8:00 PM** \nEconomc Implications of the Region Central project and Plan for Implementation - Hal Morse, Project Manager, Greater Buffalo Niagara Regional Transportation Council (GBNRTC), Professional Certification as Project Mangement Professional (PMP)\n\nThe Region Central planning project generated a proposed solution to improve mobiity, environmental improvement and economic development in the central portion of this region. In this presentation GBNRTC Project Manager Hal Morse will discuss how these factors can be integrated to generate positive improvements. Also included will be project status and the path forward to implementation.\n\nFor more information on this project, please visit the [GBNRTC website](https://www.gbnrtc.org/regioncentral).\n\n[Register for this Event](https://www.eventbrite.com/e/scajaquada-full-circle-speaker-series-tickets-965309616047)\n\nSponsored by the generosity of the Baird Foundation, City of Buffalo Common Councilmember Joseph Golombek, and the Erie County Environmental Management Council.",
        "createdAt": "2024-09-03T14:03:56.137Z",
        "updatedAt": "2024-09-03T14:38:35.538Z",
        "publishedAt": "2024-09-03T14:03:58.491Z",
        "featuredImage": {
